solution.javascript:
function binarySearch(nums, target) {
  let low = 0
  let high = nums.length - 1

  while (low <= high) {
    const mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2)
    if (nums[mid] === target) return mid
    if (nums[mid] < target) {
      low = mid + 1
    } else {
      high = mid - 1
    }
  }
  return -1
}

description.en:
Before you write any code, **predict**. This function prints a party's announcements for `n` guests:

```js
function announce(n) {
  console.log('Doors open!')
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    console.log('Welcome, guest ' + i)
  }
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    console.log('Goodbye, guest ' + i)
  }
  console.log('Doors closed!')
}
```

How many lines does `announce(3)` print? And `announce(1000)`?

Now write `countPrintedLines(n)`, which returns how many lines `announce(n)` prints. Don't call `announce` and don't loop: work out the formula, so your function answers instantly, even for a trillion guests (one test uses n = 1,000,000,000,000, and a loop that big would be stopped after 2 seconds).

Example: `countPrintedLines(3)` → `8`

Goal: O(1) time, O(1) space. And `announce` itself? Two loops in a row are O(2n), which simplifies to O(n).

description.es:
Antes de escribir código, **predice**. Esta función imprime los anuncios de una fiesta para `n` invitados:

```js
function announce(n) {
  console.log('¡Se abren las puertas!')
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    console.log('Hola, persona invitada ' + i)
  }
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    console.log('Adiós, persona invitada ' + i)
  }
  console.log('¡Se cierran las puertas!')
}
```

¿Cuántas líneas imprime `announce(3)`? ¿Y `announce(1000)`?

Ahora escribe `countPrintedLines(n)`, que devuelve cuántas líneas imprime `announce(n)`. No llames a `announce` ni uses un bucle: encuentra la fórmula, para que tu función responda al instante, incluso con un billón de invitados (una prueba usa n = 1,000,000,000,000, y un bucle tan grande se detendría después de 2 segundos).

Ejemplo: `countPrintedLines(3)` → `8`

Meta: tiempo O(1), espacio O(1). ¿Y `announce`? Dos bucles seguidos son O(2n), que se simplifica a O(n).

solution.javascript:
function countPrintedLines(n) {
  // 1 line before the loops, n welcomes, n goodbyes and 1 line after
  return 2 * n + 2
}

description.en:
At the end of the party, every guest shakes hands **once** with every other guest. This code counts the handshakes the slow way:

```js
function countHandshakesSlowly(guestCount) {
  let handshakes = 0
  for (let i = 0; i < guestCount; i++) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < guestCount; j++) {
      handshakes = handshakes + 1
    }
  }
  return handshakes
}
```

Its inner loop starts at `i + 1`, so each pair shakes hands only once. What's its Big O? And before you read on, predict `countHandshakesSlowly(4)`.

Now write `countHandshakes(guestCount)`, which returns the same number **without a loop**, so it answers instantly, even for a million guests (one test uses 1,000,000: the nested loops would need about 500 billion steps, so they'd be stopped after 2 seconds). Think about how many hands each guest shakes, and how many times that counts each handshake.

Example: `countHandshakes(4)` → `6`

Goal: O(1) time, O(1) space. The slow version does about n² / 2 steps: O(n²).

description.es:
Al final de la fiesta, cada persona invitada le da la mano **una vez** a cada una de las demás. Este código cuenta los apretones de manos de la forma lenta:

```js
function countHandshakesSlowly(guestCount) {
  let handshakes = 0
  for (let i = 0; i < guestCount; i++) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < guestCount; j++) {
      handshakes = handshakes + 1
    }
  }
  return handshakes
}
```

Su bucle de adentro empieza en `i + 1`, así que cada pareja se da la mano una sola vez. ¿Cuál es su Big O? Y antes de seguir leyendo, predice `countHandshakesSlowly(4)`.

Ahora escribe `countHandshakes(guestCount)`, que devuelve el mismo número **sin un bucle**, para que responda al instante, incluso con un millón de personas (una prueba usa 1,000,000: los bucles anidados necesitarían unos 500 mil millones de pasos, así que se detendrían después de 2 segundos). Piensa en cuántas manos estrecha cada persona, y cuántas veces se cuenta así cada apretón.

Ejemplo: `countHandshakes(4)` → `6`

Meta: tiempo O(1), espacio O(1). La versión lenta da unos n² / 2 pasos: O(n²).

solution.javascript:
function countHandshakes(guestCount) {
  // Each guest shakes guestCount - 1 hands, and that counts every handshake twice.
  return (guestCount * (guestCount - 1)) / 2
}

function countHalvings(n) {
  let halvings = 0
  let size = n
  while (size > 1) {
    size = Math.floor(size / 2)
    halvings++
  }
  return halvings
}
